      FRawStaticIndexBuffer.cs   the vertex and index buffer headers
      NaniteResources.cs         the FNaniteResources field order
      FPageStreamingState.cs     the page table entry
      FByteBulkDataHeader.cs     the Zen BulkDataMap entry

**No CUE4Parse source code is copied into this repository.** The C# was read to learn the
on-disk layout; the Python is a fresh implementation with different structure -- numpy
vectorisation over the byte planes, positions and topology only, no attribute decode -- and
it is validated against the bytes on disk rather than against CUE4Parse's output. That
validation is not a claim: the pure-Python decoder was diffed against a CUE4Parse build
over all 156 Nanite meshes of Satisfactory build 495413 and agrees on the canonical
triangle multiset of every one of them, with a maximum absolute vertex delta of 0.0 cm --
bit-exact float32 -- while emitting genuinely different arrays before canonicalisation
(11,566 of 12,817 vertex rows differ on CliffPillar_01). The two implementations are
independent and equivalent, which is what makes the port a port rather than a translation.

